{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi3x4oyAibzXnGDX8kCR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LxuFuBtL43S82iXM8DMLwZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050232__xd92716/work/DenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050232; date '+%H:%M'; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/58-about-text.js'; s=open(p).read()\nstart=s.index(\"    testing: 'One command\"); end=s.index(\"\\n\", start)\ns=s[:start]+\"\"\"    testing: 'Allowed and used: headless scripts through the engine (game.advance, input taps and holds, game.debug), a scripted playthrough of the whole game, Playwright browser checks, the AI Hub harness, screenshots for look review. One command, node test/run.mjs, runs 27 headless suites (264 checks: renderer math, route compiler, physics check values, signals and ATS, limits, stations and judgments, calls and horn, timetable calibration, scoring, crowds, events, light, cameras, HUD layout at 3 screen sizes, input and glyphs, sound, voices, story, autopilot, attract, Dev Mode, progress, settings, screens, a mock AI Hub, the duel, and the full playthrough) in parallel and prints only failures and a count; --browser --hub --bundle adds 14 Playwright checks and the 3 AI Hub harness runs on the final file',\"\"\"+s[end:]\nstart=s.index(\"    usage: 'unknown'\"); end=s.index(\"\\n\", start)\ns=s[:start]+\"\"\"    usage: 'API cost: unknown; tokens: unknown; session time: about 3 hours (05:02 to about 08:05 by the machine clock)'\"\"\"+s[end:]\nstart=s.index(\"  testingFeedback: [\"); end=s.index(\"  ],\", start)+4\ns=s[:start]+\"\"\"  testingFeedback: [\n    'How many issues did testing catch? About 40, all fixed before shipping: 23 from the headless suites and the autopilot runs (among them a scripted freight that never stopped, a standing start that could not move the train on P1, an arrival estimator that was always late and then always early, signal lookups that walked the loop in route order, grade easing that lost height, beacons not reset by a jump, a missing holding brake, comfort drained by the autopilot, a starting Halo Time that ignored the run\\\\'s difficulty, an obstruction that never cleared, the HUD and tips spilling off 320 and 427 px screens, storage with no memory fallback), 15 from screenshot review (ground drawn over the ballast, a viaduct with no deck, a tunnel portal that painted the whole sky, people and lamp glows never drawn, overlapping title, results and duel layouts) and 1 from the browser checks (a menu click that only picked the focused row); plus 3 mistakes in the tests themselves.',\n    'How many would be considered critical or game breaking? 8: the S2 freight deadlock (S2 could not be finished), the P1 standing start (the tutorial\\\\'s first step was impossible), the plan\\\\'s timetables (good drivers ran out of Halo Time), the obstruction that never cleared for a train stopped far back (S3 stuck), a name clash that crashed attract mode, a missing route helper that crashed every call, the signal lookup that skipped the terminal\\\\'s restricted speed, and people and lamp glows that were never drawn.',\n    'What was the most helpful test you ran? Driving every stage headless with the autopilot and printing each event with the clock. It found the freight deadlock, the signal ordering, the timetable and scoring problems in seconds, and it grew into the scripted playthrough of the whole game.',\n    'What was the least helpful test you ran? Three early checks in the HUD and screens suites that only asserted true (I made them real later), and the first serial run of the suite, which took over 15 minutes until it was split across worker processes.'\n  ],\n\"\"\"+s[end:]\nstart=s.index(\"  engineFeedback: [\"); end=s.index(\"  ],\", start)+4\ns=s[:start]+\"\"\"  engineFeedback: [\n    'What did you like most about the engine? Its headless determinism: game.advance with exact fixed steps, input taps and game.debug made a 30-minute career testable in seconds, and the Humanoid rigs, the Shell\\\\'s menus and settings, and the chip synth meant a whole cast, every menu screen and all the sound needed no assets.',\n    'Did you get stuck or guess wrong? The ROAD module projects heights with half the screen height, which squashes the world on wide screens, and it has no multiple tracks, raised strips or rear cameras, so I forked it into a new renderer. I guessed the yaw for rigs drawn in my own view, assumed the Menu could scale its text (it can\\\\'t, so I wrote a larger one), and did not expect E.store to have no memory fallback when localStorage is missing (headless tests, blocked storage).',\n    'What was the most important thing you had to build yourself? The rail renderer (square-pixel pseudo-3D with several tracks, strips with faces and patterns, point things, crest clipping, rear views, fog and time-of-day tinting), and on top of it the train dynamics and the model-predictive autopilot that drives attract mode, the tests and the timetable calibration.',\n    'What was the hardest part about using the engine? Finding the internals the API card does not cover (the Shell\\\\'s settings rows, the audio buses, the pose solver, the Dialog\\\\'s typing) in a 14,700-line file; the API index helped, but several features needed reading and patching the source.',\n    'What did you change in the engine, and why? A Dialog voice hook (per-character gibberish voices), a settings-screen group filter with Reset (Dev Mode\\\\'s live sliders, hidden from the standard Settings), PlayStation glyphs by default plus face-button and menu glyphs in the font, audio bus accessors (the continuous train synth follows volume and ducking), bow, point and flag poses (staff, workers, the finale), and the hub\\\\'s Create+Options rule in the pad reader; plus the new rail.js module. Each is listed in ENGINE-CHANGES.md.',\n    'If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be? Ship a general pseudo-3D strip renderer (or make ROAD square-pixel with lateral objects and rear views), because vehicle games beyond OutRun need platforms, trains and buildings beside the line.'\n  ],\n\"\"\"+s[end:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode -e \"import('./test/lib.mjs').then(({ load }) => { const { DH } = load(); console.log(DH.ABOUT.testingFeedback.length, DH.ABOUT.engineFeedback.length, DH.ABOUT.promptFeedback.length, DH.ABOUT.sourceInformation.usage); })\"","description":"Write the final About and feedback text"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2117,"cache_read_input_tokens":926917,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2117},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b1bf799-1946-4a15-a1b7-75e4a7d99d2e","uuid":"aba2c730-0480-4c5b-b3b0-b11ff82d1383","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:33:26.297Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi3x4MvxAkTG9dugVAsS","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LxuFuBtL43S82iXM8DMLwZ":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050232__xd92716/work/DenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050232; date '+%H:%M'; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/58-about-text.js'; s=open(p).read()\nstart=s.index(\"    testing: 'One command\"); end=s.index(\"\\n\", start)\ns=s[:start]+\"\"\"    testing: 'Allowed and used: headless scripts through the engine (game.advance, input taps and holds, game.debug), a scripted playthrough of the whole game, Playwright browser checks, the AI Hub harness, screenshots for look review. One command, node test/run.mjs, runs 27 headless suites (264 checks: renderer math, route compiler, physics check values, signals and ATS, limits, stations and judgments, calls and horn, timetable calibration, scoring, crowds, events, light, cameras, HUD layout at 3 screen sizes, input and glyphs, sound, voices, story, autopilot, attract, Dev Mode, progress, settings, screens, a mock AI Hub, the duel, and the full playthrough) in parallel and prints only failures and a count; --browser --hub --bundle adds 14 Playwright checks and the 3 AI Hub harness runs on the final file',\"\"\"+s[end:]\nstart=s.index(\"    usage: 'unknown'\"); end=s.index(\"\\n\", start)\ns=s[:start]+\"\"\"    usage: 'API cost: unknown; tokens: unknown; session time: about 3 hours (05:02 to about 08:05 by the machine clock)'\"\"\"+s[end:]\nstart=s.index(\"  testingFeedback: [\"); end=s.index(\"  ],\", start)+4\ns=s[:start]+\"\"\"  testingFeedback: [\n    'How many issues did testing catch? About 40, all fixed before shipping: 23 from the headless suites and the autopilot runs (among them a scripted freight that never stopped, a standing start that could not move the train on P1, an arrival estimator that was always late and then always early, signal lookups that walked the loop in route order, grade easing that lost height, beacons not reset by a jump, a missing holding brake, comfort drained by the autopilot, a starting Halo Time that ignored the run\\\\'s difficulty, an obstruction that never cleared, the HUD and tips spilling off 320 and 427 px screens, storage with no memory fallback), 15 from screenshot review (ground drawn over the ballast, a viaduct with no deck, a tunnel portal that painted the whole sky, people and lamp glows never drawn, overlapping title, results and duel layouts) and 1 from the browser checks (a menu click that only picked the focused row); plus 3 mistakes in the tests themselves.',\n    'How many would be considered critical or game breaking? 8: the S2 freight deadlock (S2 could not be finished), the P1 standing start (the tutorial\\\\'s first step was impossible), the plan\\\\'s timetables (good drivers ran out of Halo Time), the obstruction that never cleared for a train stopped far back (S3 stuck), a name clash that crashed attract mode, a missing route helper that crashed every call, the signal lookup that skipped the terminal\\\\'s restricted speed, and people and lamp glows that were never drawn.',\n    'What was the most helpful test you ran? Driving every stage headless with the autopilot and printing each event with the clock. It found the freight deadlock, the signal ordering, the timetable and scoring problems in seconds, and it grew into the scripted playthrough of the whole game.',\n    'What was the least helpful test you ran? Three early checks in the HUD and screens suites that only asserted true (I made them real later), and the first serial run of the suite, which took over 15 minutes until it was split across worker processes.'\n  ],\n\"\"\"+s[end:]\nstart=s.index(\"  engineFeedback: [\"); end=s.index(\"  ],\", start)+4\ns=s[:start]+\"\"\"  engineFeedback: [\n    'What did you like most about the engine? Its headless determinism: game.advance with exact fixed steps, input taps and game.debug made a 30-minute career testable in seconds, and the Humanoid rigs, the Shell\\\\'s menus and settings, and the chip synth meant a whole cast, every menu screen and all the sound needed no assets.',\n    'Did you get stuck or guess wrong? The ROAD module projects heights with half the screen height, which squashes the world on wide screens, and it has no multiple tracks, raised strips or rear cameras, so I forked it into a new renderer. I guessed the yaw for rigs drawn in my own view, assumed the Menu could scale its text (it can\\\\'t, so I wrote a larger one), and did not expect E.store to have no memory fallback when localStorage is missing (headless tests, blocked storage).',\n    'What was the most important thing you had to build yourself? The rail renderer (square-pixel pseudo-3D with several tracks, strips with faces and patterns, point things, crest clipping, rear views, fog and time-of-day tinting), and on top of it the train dynamics and the model-predictive autopilot that drives attract mode, the tests and the timetable calibration.',\n    'What was the hardest part about using the engine? Finding the internals the API card does not cover (the Shell\\\\'s settings rows, the audio buses, the pose solver, the Dialog\\\\'s typing) in a 14,700-line file; the API index helped, but several features needed reading and patching the source.',\n    'What did you change in the engine, and why? A Dialog voice hook (per-character gibberish voices), a settings-screen group filter with Reset (Dev Mode\\\\'s live sliders, hidden from the standard Settings), PlayStation glyphs by default plus face-button and menu glyphs in the font, audio bus accessors (the continuous train synth follows volume and ducking), bow, point and flag poses (staff, workers, the finale), and the hub\\\\'s Create+Options rule in the pad reader; plus the new rail.js module. Each is listed in ENGINE-CHANGES.md.',\n    'If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be? Ship a general pseudo-3D strip renderer (or make ROAD square-pixel with lateral objects and rear views), because vehicle games beyond OutRun need platforms, trains and buildings beside the line.'\n  ],\n\"\"\"+s[end:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode -e \"import('./test/lib.mjs').then(({ load }) => { const { DH } = load(); console.log(DH.ABOUT.testingFeedback.length, DH.ABOUT.engineFeedback.length, DH.ABOUT.promptFeedback.length, DH.ABOUT.sourceInformation.usage); })\"","description":"Write the final About and feedback text"}}}
