{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Read, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - The user invoked `/goal` with this condition (enforced by a session Stop hook): \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.\"\n   - STAGE.md: read TASK.md (what to build) and PLAN.md (how, by claude-opus-5-5 max); build the game following the plan using its title (**Densha de Halo!**, GameTitle=DenshaDeHalo, SOURCE=DenshaDeGo); TASK.md wins on conflicts; deliver its file name and reply sections.\n   - TASK.md essentials: source Densha de Go!; build on my-3d2dge dist/handoff; single html `DenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050232.html` in root; dev subfolder `DenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050232/`; all audio in code, Animalese/Simlish gibberish voices; AI Hub (lib/hub) multiplayer + game on its own; Dev Mode from pause menu with live balance sliders + reset; attract mode after 10 s idle (any input exits); 10-foot controller-first UI, PlayStation glyphs w/ Xbox option, keyboard/mouse native, hover moves focus; touch-only devices: no touch controls, show \"Controller or keyboard required\" + settings button, attract still runs; narrative tone like source; no TODOs/placeholders/stubs; About/Credits screen + chat reply with Source Information (Date 2026-11-04 05:02:32, Source, Plan, Genre and Perspective, Tech, Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\", Model \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\", Usage), Testing Feedback (4 Qs), Engine Feedback (6 Qs), Prompt Feedback (4 Qs); exit-interview.json in exact shape incl. aiHub block.\n   - Security/process constraints (verbatim from TASK.md): \"Do not read files outside what you need - other agents share this directory. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\" Also: \"Keep them [tests] behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\"\n   - Stop hook feedback #1: wanted end-to-end evidence for the Xbox glyph option in a browser, the Duel keyboard halves, and Dev Mode sound board / Trigger an event. (Done: 32 browser checks; 299 passed.)\n   - Stop hook feedback #2 (most recent): \"the 'Trigger an event' and sound board were only exercised after the final suite. The Dev Mode 'Trigger an event' tool never fired at a station or with the drive frozen... TASK.md items such as the 'Trigger an event' tool and Dev Mode's full tool list were not all shown to work end to end, and the transcript does not show a full check of every TASK.md item against the bundle.\"\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - my-3D2dge v0.85.2 full engine (2D), E.Game headless/`game.advance` fixed 1/120 steps, scenes, E.Shell HTML pause/settings/controls, E.Dialog, Humanoid/Blob rigs, ChipAudio, E.store (localStorage), input.label/glyphs, game.players/allowJoin/addPlayer({keys:'right'})/splitScreen, Input.halfKeys.\n   - New pseudo-3D rail renderer (square-pixel projection: sy uses hw), 5 m segments, strips with faces/patterns (F.rect), point things, crest clipping, rear views (dir −1 mirrors curve and x), fog/time-of-day tint cache, deck for viaducts/bridges, tunnel portal hill mound.\n   - Designer route scripts `[s, command, params]` compiled; station kit; seeded zone scenery.\n   - Train dynamics in km/h & km/h/s (lag τ, resistance, grade −0.0353·‰, adhesion, slip/slide, holding brake, stiction 0.15), check values (0–80 P5 30.4 s; B4 39.2 s/439 m; EB 181 m; coast −8.2 km/h/min; brakeScale×2 → 232 m).\n   - Run rule engine (signals 4-lamp aspects R/Y/YG/G/YY, ATS bell/confirm/EB, SPAD, limits over train length, stations judgment table, dwell sequence, calls window 180/30 m sweet 120–60, horn zones, Halo Time, comfort, checkpoints), events, tutorial.\n   - Autopilot: braking-curve planner, model-predictive final stop, timetable cruise cap by bisection over a simulated arrival (with analytic final creep), min-time mode, delay foresight; tutorial uses mintime; calibration tool sets arr = par+9 s rounded to 5 s.\n   - AI Hub Session Protocol 1 ghost mode, own card, ready() with no key, progress/result/time-up/end; harness via python http.server port 0.\n   - Tests: vm-loaded headless suites, parallel worker processes, Playwright browser checks, hub harness; screenshots.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (dev folder D = /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050232__xd92716/work/DenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050232):\n   - Root deliverables: `../DenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050232.html` (1680 KB, 34 inline scripts, `<meta charset>` then unmodified session.js first, hub tags incl. `hub:session-minutes` 6, `<title>Densha de Halo!</title>`), `../exit-interview.json` (validated; 15 sourceInformation keys, 4/6/4 feedback, aiHub tags first-person,vehicles,arcade,retro,versus,story).\n   - `engine/my-3d2dge.js` (patched, logged in ENGINE-CHANGES.md items 1–7): Dialog voice function hook (`const txt = this._page.join(' '); ... this.voice(txt[k], k, txt, this)`), `_settingsRows(add, only)` + `s.groups` + 'Reset to defaults' button and 'Dev' hidden from standard settings, glyphs default 'playstation', font glyphs ✕ ○ □ △ ◂ ·, `audio.bus(name)`/`audio.noiseBuffer()`, poses bow/point/flag in poseW + solver, hub Create(Pad8)+Options(Pad9) rule in Input.tick.\n   - `engine/modules/rail.js`: Rail class; `_place` fixed for point things:\n     ```js\n     _place(map, it) {\n       if (it.s0 === undefined) { const j = this.segAt(it.s); let l = map.get(j); if (!l) map.set(j, l = []); l.push(it); return; }   // a point thing\n       ...\n     ```\n     ground at gy−0.45; deck quad when `sg.deck`; `_face` supports col null; near face `dir > 0 ? F.end : (F.end2 || F.end)`.\n   - `src/00-core.js`: DH namespace, game creation with `menu: { items: menuItems, settings: GAME_SETTINGS, controls: DH.CONTROL_NAMES, quit: 'title' }`, KEYS (up/down lever, power Pad7, brake Pad6, neutral KeyN/Pad5, eb Backspace/KeyX/Pad4, call KeyE/Mouse0/Pad0, horn Space/Pad2, ats KeyQ/Pad3, view KeyC/Pad1, dbg Backquote), DUEL_KEYS order call,horn,ats,eb,neutral,view, DH.store with in-memory MEM fallback, DH.touchOnly (forceTouchOnly override), DH.leverUp.\n   - `src/01-tuning.js`: 19 sliders as settings `dev_<key>` group 'Dev', DH.resetTuning, DH.DIFF easy/normal/expert, DH.guideOn.\n   - `src/20-routes.js` (HALO loop + DEPOT scripts), `21-route-compiler.js` (R.wrap, centred grade easing, station track shifts injected, loop seam track carry, validate), `21b-route-builders.js` (buildStation/Tunnel/Bridge/Viaduct/Crossing/Workers, autoScenery with fences/roads/fields; posters at platform edges).\n   - `src/22-stages.js` (S0–S5, PR, story, TUTORIAL steps, CHARS, FINALE, POSTCARDS; workers event uses `site: 'WK1'`), `23-timetable.js` (calibrated).\n   - `src/30-train.js`: trainStep with hold brake and standing branch `if (Math.abs(drive) > B + .15) { a = drive - Math.sign(drive) * B; st.v = v + a * dt; }`.\n   - `src/31-run.js`: Run class (reset, step order, signalsAhead, _aspects, ATS, limits, stations/_judge/_settle/backup/_startDwell/_dwellStep, calls, horn, checkpoints, snapshot, seg(), N(), U(); grace from `this.diff.grace`).\n   - `src/34-events.js`: Events (trigger(type) for Dev: doorRush requires dwell; ats rings next signal; obstruction stopped condition d<1200; workers by e.site), HANDLERS (radio, oncoming, freight with path Y→A→LP, rival, doorRush, festival, fog, glare, obstruction, workers, flash, kota, fuji, finale), Tutorial (getter renamed `cur`, retry, reopen lapsed call).\n   - `src/35-autopilot.js`: Autopilot (mode default `run.stage.tutorial ? 'mintime' : 'timetable'`), profile, simArrival, pickCap, delayAhead, finalStop; DH.autoRun, DH.proof.\n   - `src/40-sound.js`, `41-babble.js` (sound synth, SFX, melodies, songs; Babble syllabify/say, DH.dialogVoice).\n   - `src/50-cab.js` (dash 3×3 lamp/button block, narrow layout), `51-hud.js`, `52-story.js` (tips wrap), `55-ui-core.js` (BigMenu: click on any row picks it; drawScenic; idleTick; Progress; stageCard 2-line stops; showHelp), `56-ui-front.js` (title, DH.titleMenu, haloMap, DH.mapSel, freeRun, briefing), `57-ui-end.js` (results, gameOver, ending w/ bowing crowd & cancel skip, driversLog postcards, about), `58-about-text.js` (DH.ABOUT single source; usage \"API cost: unknown; tokens: unknown; session time: about 3 hours (05:02 to about 08:05 by the machine clock)\"; testing text mentions 264 headless checks and \"32 Playwright checks (... the duel\\'s keyboard halves, Dev Mode\\'s event triggers, sound board and live sliders) and the 3 AI Hub harness runs\" — apostrophes MUST be escaped), `60-drive.js` (Drive class, DH.wheelQ, pauseItems with 'Retry stage', 'Retry from last station', 'Dev Mode', 'How to Drive'; none in hub), `61-attract.js` (teleport/jumpToStop/skipBefore, vignettes, pointer-move exit), `62-dev.js` (DH.Dev tools listed below), `63-hub.js`, `64-duel.js` (DH.duelDrives exposed), `90-gallery.js`, `99-start.js` (deep links incl. `#duel=auto`, game.debug handle).\n   - `62-dev.js` button labels: 'Auto-drive: ON/OFF', 'Autopilot skill: 1', 'God mode: …', 'Freeze Halo Time: …', 'Time scale: 1×', 'Jump: next station approach (600 m)', 'Jump to km 1.0 (change)', 'Go to km 1.0', 'Skip to the next stop (PERFECT)', 'Finish the stage (perfect)', 'Fail the stage (game over)', 'Time of day: …', 'Weather: CLEAR', 'Force the next signal: …', 'Trigger an event…' (EVENTS = [['ats','ATS TEST'],['obstruction','OBSTRUCTION'],['doorRush','DOOR RUSH'],['oncoming','ONCOMING TRAIN'],['workers','TRACK WORKERS'],['flash','HEADLIGHT FLASH']] + 'Back'), 'Camera: CAB', 'Debug overlay: OFF  (` key)', 'Braking guide: …', 'Balance sliders…', 'Sound board…', 'Unlock all stages', 'Reset save data…' (devReset screen: 'Keep my save', 'Erase it'), 'Back'.\n   - `test/run.mjs`: parent spawns workers `--worker=<suite>` (K = min(suites, cpus−1, 8)), aggregates `RESULT p f`, then `--browser`/`--hub`/`--bundle`; prints `N passed, M failed`.\n   - `test/browser.mjs`: `open(opts, hash)` helper; checks title, attract 10.5 s, key returns, keyboard to drive & W powers, mouse hover/click (aims at `DH.titleMenu.box[3]`), touch-only phone, minute of auto driving, PlayStation/Xbox labels (`Cross,Square,Triangle,R2 / L2` and `A,X,Y,RT / LT,A`), keyboard switch back, duel halves (P1 `F G H R T Y W`, P2 `. / , L ; ' ↑`), waits `d.run.pilot && d.run.dwell && d.run.dwell.sigClear` then W drives P1 only and ArrowUp drives P2, Dev Mode via buttons: Trigger ONCOMING TRAIN (actors include oncoming*), ATS TEST rings, Sound board (SFX chime, Melody akari, Song march, Voice hoshino), Back `.first()`, Balance sliders count 19, fill nth(1)=2 → TUNING.brakeScale 2, Reset to defaults → 1. Screenshots shots/xbox-prompts.png, duel-keys.png, dev-soundboard.png, dev-balance.png.\n   - `test/hub-harness.mjs` (copies harness files + bundle as game.html into test/.serve, python http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1, verifies title, runs 3 scenarios, kills server by PID, deletes .serve), `test/lib.mjs`, `suites-core.mjs`, `suites-ui.mjs`, `playthrough.mjs`.\n   - `tools/gen-index.mjs`, `tools/bundle.mjs`, `tools/calibrate.mjs`, `tools/exit-interview.mjs`, `tools/shots.mjs`, `tools/shot.mjs`; README.md; ENGINE-CHANGES.md.\n\n4. Errors and fixes (major ones):\n   - Ballast hidden by ground (ground to gy−0.45); viaduct pit (deck); portal painted whole sky (hill mound); strip wrap sign; rear end face selection.\n   - Grade easing lost height (centred ramps); loop seam track positions; home signals inside platforms; depot platform too short.\n   - Freight never stopped (actor stop condition `d <= .1 && v < .5` with min crawl); signal lookups in route order past seam (signalsAhead sorted); simArrival never arriving/pessimistic (analytic final creep with B1); freight foresight (delayAhead); comfort drain (jerk-based); maxScore missing optional calls/flash; standing start bug `st.v = a*dt` → `v + a*dt` (tutorial couldn't start on P1); stiction 0.15 for closure slope creep; holding brake during doors; tutorial crawl (mintime); difficulty grace; obstruction stopped distance; workers site id; beacon flags on teleport; tutorial getter vs method clash (`get step` → `get cur`); R.wrap missing; storage memory fallback; attract pointer exit; HUD/tip overflow; dash layout; title/results/duel/minimal HUD/demo overlaps; notch readout color; wipers; postcard counter; ellipsis glyph; BigMenu click picks any row; dynamic point things never drawn (`_place`).\n   - Test issues: fade timing, horn location, crowd test (20% stay), headless menu boxes (draw into recorder), ATS timing, canvas locator `#screen`, click gap, duel departure wait, 'Back' ambiguity.\n 