ency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":354,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Densha de Halo!** is done: the single file `DenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050232.html` (1.7 MB) and `exit-interview.json` are in the root, and the dev files are in the subfolder of the same name. The last full run of `node test/run.mjs --browser --hub --bundle`, on the final bundle, gave **377 passed, 0 failed**.\n\n**What changed in this last stretch**\n- **Dev Mode's \"Trigger an event\" now works anywhere.** A triggered obstruction picks the next level crossing ahead. Track workers set up a work site far enough ahead to brake down to 25, with its crew, lookout, boards and slow order. Triggered events no longer jump to their scripted places in the stage.\n- **One Dev Mode bug fixed.** \"Skip to the next stop\" judged one stop and also skipped past the next one, so \"Finish the stage\" could finish without judging every stop. It now judges each stop in turn.\n- **An obstruction triggered at a standstill** only counts as avoided once the train has moved and then stopped short of it.\n- **New browser checks for every Dev Mode tool, each pressed through its own button on the bundle.** On S1, the drive is paused in the dwell at Akari Central with Freeze Halo Time on. There I fire all six events: door rush, obstruction, track workers, headlight flash, oncoming train and ATS test. Auto-drive then handles every one: the doors reopen, it stops short of the blocked crossing, keeps to 25 through the work, answers the flash and confirms the ATS. Halo Time doesn't change through any of it. The other tools are covered too (skill, god mode, time scale, both jumps, skip, finish, time of day, weather, forced signal, camera, debug overlay, braking guide, unlock all, both reset choices, fail).\n- **New checks of the deliverables against TASK.md** (`test/bundle-checks.mjs`), 21 in all. They cover:\n  - the file name;\n  - the hub client first and byte-for-byte unmodified, and the hub tags;\n  - nothing loaded from outside, and no audio or image files;\n  - every source file inlined as it is now;\n  - no TODO, placeholder or stub words;\n  - the exit interview's exact shape, and that the About screen shows the same text.\n- **Engine build stamp.** The last check found the engine's unstamped `'dev-build'` label in its build line, so it is now `'densha-de-halo 2026-11-04'`. This is logged as item 8 in ENGINE-CHANGES.md.\n\n**TASK.md item by item, and what checks it**\n\n| TASK.md item | What checks it |\n|---|---|\n| Single .html in the root, dev subfolder of the same name | bundle checks |\n| Built on my-3d2dge handoff; engine edits allowed | engine v0.85.2, 8 edits listed in ENGINE-CHANGES.md, plus the new rail renderer |\n| All audio in code, gibberish voices | \"no audio files\" bundle check; sound and voice suites; sound board pressed in the browser |\n| AI Hub multiplayer, and the game on its own | 3 runs in the real hub test harness; mock-hub suite; hub client and tags checked in the bundle |\n| Dev Mode from the pause menu, live sliders with reset | 2 headless suites; all Dev Mode tools through their buttons in the browser; 19 sliders plus Reset |\n| Attract mode after 10 s, any input exits | browser (10.5 s idle, then a key press) and the headless attract suite |\n| Controller-first UI, PlayStation glyphs with an Xbox option, native keyboard and mouse, hover moves focus | browser glyph, keyboard and mouse checks; headless input suite |\n| Touch-only devices | browser phone check: \"Controller or keyboard required\" with Settings, and attract still runs |\n| Feature-complete demo | scripted playthrough: tutorial passed, S1–S5 ranked S, the ending, all 8 postcards, every event |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | bundle checks on the game's code and the whole bundle |\n| About/Credits screen and exit-interview.json | bundle checks: same text on both, 15 labels, 4/6/4 ans